# Input graph `in_first` for BD2KOnFHIR__fhirtordf__..._fhir_decimal_issue_filter
# — written during translation, against the region.  Its counterpart is
# fixture_second.ttl (`in_second`); `in_both` starts empty.
#
# What each subject exercises (see fixture_second.ttl for the other side):
#   obs1, obs2  xsd:decimal on both sides, equal value, different lexical form
#               -> the case the filter exists for: moved to in_both, removed here
#   obs8        xsd:decimal on both sides, identical term -> also moved
#   obs3        xsd:decimal on both sides, DIFFERENT value -> nothing moves
#   obs4        no (s, p) at all in in_second -> in_second.value() is None
#               (the zero-solution case that .first() must answer None too)
#   obs5        xsd:integer on both sides -> neighbouring datatype, must not match
#   obs6        plain literal -> must not match
#   obs7        a URIRef object -> isinstance(o, Literal) must reject it
#   the bnode   a decimal under a blank subject with no counterpart -> None again
#   Neighbours that share a TERM of a moved triple but not the whole triple, so a
#   removal whose bound term was widened to a wildcard would also delete them:
#   obs1 ex:alt   same subject and same object as the moved obs1 pair, other predicate
#   obs10         same predicate and same object as the moved obs1 pair, other subject
#   obs14         same subject and predicate as a moved pair, another object (8.5)
#   obs15         6.000, facing TWO equal decimals in in_second (see fixture_second.ttl)
#   obs12, obs13  a decimal facing an integer of equal numeric value
#                 (Decimal(2) == 2): the datatype tests, not the values, reject them
@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex:obs1 ex:value "1.0"^^xsd:decimal .
